# Flutter map — generated for {{ public }}

`lib/config.dart` is pre-wired to your server and the same layers as the web map.

```bash
cd mobile/flutter
flutter create --project-name {{ project }}_map --org ge.gisstack .   # adds android/ ios/ (keeps lib/)
flutter pub get
flutter run
```

* Language switch KA/EN in the app bar (remembered on the device); layers in the drawer.
* Release builds on Android need the `INTERNET` permission in
  `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`:
  `<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET"/>`
{% if tls == 'none' %}
* Your server is plain HTTP: add `android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"` to `<application>` and the
  matching ATS exception on iOS — or switch the installer to HTTPS.
{% endif %}
* The code targets the `flutter_map` 6–8 API (`MapOptions(initialCenter: …)`). If a newer major
  release changes it, pin `flutter_map` in `pubspec.yaml`.
